  ],
  "text": "Cooking is not about flavour. It is digestion you do outside your body. A big gut and a big brain are both enormously expensive. Almost nothing affords both. A great ape spends most of its waking hours chewing. You spend under an hour a day eating, and you get more calories out of it. Heat breaks the tough structure apart before it ever reaches you. So the gut had less work to do, and a smaller gut is much cheaper to run. That freed up energy, and the fossil record shows exactly where it went. Guts shrink. Skulls grow. Teeth get smaller. All of it at once. And no other animal cooks. Not a single one. All those hours you were not chewing became the first free time anyone ever had. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
